  "id": "animal-social-behavior",
  "term": "animal social behavior",
  "definition": "Animal social behavior is the study of how animals organize their relationships and living arrangements with others of the same species, such as living alone or in groups. It examines how ecological and demographic conditions, including population density and major environmental changes, shape patterns of spatial and social organization.",
